<section style="padding:3rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Why Partner with SDF Clothing?</h2><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">We offer yarn dyeing, piece dyeing, and garment dyeing from the same facility, letting you choose the method that suits your design rather than being limited to whichever one a subcontractor happens to specialize in. Yarn dyeing suits stripes and jacquards where color needs to be set before construction; garment dyeing suits solid-color pieces where a softer, worn-in hand feel is the goal. GOTS, OEKO-TEX Standard 100, BSCI, WRAP, and ISO 9001 certification cover the facility.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Each dyeing method carries a different cost and lead-time profile — garment dyeing typically adds the least time since it happens after construction, while yarn dyeing adds time upfront but enables patterns piece dyeing can't achieve. Minimum order is 300 pieces per style, with lab dip approval, bulk dyeing, and export documentation included.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">However you dye it — yarn, piece, or garment — the finished apparel carries Bangladesh's trade terms into your landed cost: a 20% US tariff cap from late 2025, well below the Section 301 exposure Chinese-dyed goods face, and EU duty-free access under Everything But Arms through November 2029 despite this year's LDC graduation.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem">Ready to start? <a href="/contact" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Request a sample</a> or <a href="/contact" style="color:var(--color-primary)">contact our team</a> for a detailed FOB quote within 48 hours.</p></div></section>
